CVE_context:
According to https://www.slf4j.org/log4shell.html , 
{quote}
..., log4j 1.x comes with JMSAppender which will perform a JNDI lookup if enabled in log4j's configuration file, i.e. log4j.properties or log4j.xml.
{quote}
Therefore, it is better to exclude JMSAppender.class from the generated jar.

See also [CVE-2021-4104|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-4104].

I cannot upgrade to the latest version due to historical issues,
Excuse me ，CVE-2024-25710 and CVE-2024-26308 Whether the SevenZArchiveEntry and SevenZFile classes for 7z decompression are involved.

org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.sevenz.SevenZArchiveEntry;
org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.sevenz.SevenZFile;

