Review Comment:
   You aren't caching the credentials, so this will get logged very very often.

both of the CVEs are unlikely to affect Solr. 

From CVE-2022-42004
{quote}An application is vulnerable only with certain customized choices for deserialization.{quote}

From CVE-2022-42003
{quote}when the UNWRAP_SINGLE_VALUE_ARRAYS feature is enabled{quote}

Either way will look at Jackson upgrade - https://github.com/apache/solr/blob/main/versions.props#L5 needs to be updated to 2.13.4.20221013

Like CVE-2014-3628 , the vulnerability also exists in Admin UI Schema-Browser page and Analysis page, which was caused by  improper validation of user-supplied input, for example, create fields by Schema API.  When the Schema-Browser page or Analysis page url is clicked,  an XSS will be triggered. An attacker could use this vulnerability to steal the victim's cookie-based authentication credentials. 
